      <li><strong>Louder alarms</strong> jolt you with cortisol — and still get snoozed.</li>
      <li><strong>More caffeine</strong> masks the tiredness and wrecks the next night.</li>
      <li><strong>Sleeping pills</strong> knock you out but leave you groggier, not rested.</li>
    </ul>
